# Trivy misconfiguration suppressions for rocm-examples.
#
# DS-0002 "Specify at least 1 USER command ... with non-root user":
# Every Dockerfile in this repo produces a GitHub Actions job-container image
# (see .github/workflows/build_*.yml `container:`). A non-root USER cannot
# write GITHUB_WORKSPACE, which is host-mounted and owned by the runner uid;
# that breaks actions/checkout and every subsequent build step. This was
# verified empirically by running the exact CI build steps against a non-root
# image. These images must run as root, so the finding does not apply here.
AVD-DS-0002
#
# DS-0029 "'--no-install-recommends' flag is missed" on `apt-get install -y rocm`:
# `rocm` is a meta-package whose recommended dependencies pull in the ROCm
# runtime/toolchain subcomponents the image needs. Adding --no-install-recommends
# would drop those recommends and produce an incomplete image, so the flag is
# intentionally omitted for the meta-package install.
AVD-DS-0029
